{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BraneTowerZHabiro","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BraneTowerZHabiro","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.no_uniform_phi_proj_recovers_ame_at_threshold_10pct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.no_uniform_phi_proj_recovers_ame_at_threshold_10pct","kind":"theorem","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L477-L498","doc":"**No-uniform-n_⋆ corollary.**  The witness-recorded best-case\nerror on tritium under the operator-valued form is `5.49` MeV,\nwhich exceeds the 10% AME-threshold of `0.848` MeV.\n\nPer the structure of `RecoversWithRelativeError eps B_target` in\n`BraneTowerNStar.lean`, satisfaction requires\n`|Phi_proj - B_target| ≤ eps · |B_target|`.  The witness data\nshows the best `Phi_proj` we can extract from the operator-\nvalued probe at tritium is `2.9896` MeV (B_op at k=1), which\nleaves `|2.9896 - 8.4818| = 5.49` MeV vs threshold\n`0.10 · 8.4818 = 0.848` MeV — fails.\n\nCombined with the analogous failures on D and ³He at other\nuniform `k`, this is the formal Lean-level statement that the\nAME mass-binding sector's brane-tower-transient component\ndoes NOT close uniformly under any of the six probed\noperator-volume conventions — the conclusion the six-way\nrefutation chain delivers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.operator_tower_violates_tritium_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.operator_tower_violates_tritium_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L467-L475","doc":"The witness-recorded best-case error on tritium exceeds the\n10% threshold — refuting `RecoversWithRelativeError` for the\noperator-valued tower at any `Phi_proj` value within the\n`B_op` range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessTritiumBestKOneOpAbsErrMeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessTritiumBestKOneOpAbsErrMeV","kind":"def","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L455-L465","doc":"**Threshold-violation by the per-eigenvalue operator-valued\ntower at tritium under any uniform `k`.**\n\nThe best uniform `k = 1` gives `tritium err = -64.75%` of\nAME = 8.4818 MeV → `|Phi_proj - AME_T| ≈ 5.49` MeV, which\nEXCEEDS `0.10 · 8.4818 = 0.848` MeV.\n\nWitness: probe-phiq-operator-valued.witness.json, atom = tritium,\nk = 1: B_op = 2.9896 MeV, AME = 8.4818 MeV, |Δ| = 5.49 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.thresholdTritium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.thresholdTritium","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L451-L453","doc":"The 10% relative-error threshold from\n`RecoversWithRelativeError` instantiated at AME tritium. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ameHelium3MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ameHelium3MeV","kind":"def","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L449-L449","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ameTritiumMeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ameTritiumMeV","kind":"def","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L448-L448","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ameDeuteronMeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ameDeuteronMeV","kind":"def","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L446-L447","doc":"Witness-recorded AME light-isotope binding energies (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nStar_all_probed_forms_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nStar_all_probed_forms_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L382-L419","doc":"**All probed `n_⋆` families refuted.** Combining the two\nscalar-eigenvalue refutations with the canonical\noperator-valued (per-eigenvalue, signed, operator-trace,\nWedderburn-weighted) refutation, the substrate-derived\nmultiplicity / Type-B-folded-crystal-depth refutation, AND the\npair-knot product-volume magic-shell refutation: every\nempirically probed form of the `n_⋆` existence claim on\n`conj:brane-tower-z-habiro` fails the `10%` falsifiability\nthreshold.\n\nWhat survives the closure (open):\n* the algebraic Cauchy-limit half of the conjecture (untouched);\n* the ³He binding gap itself (structural deficit; not a\n  level-selection failure) — see sibling `.md`\n  §\"Pair-knot magic-shell probe\" for the LP-dual confirmation\n  that the pair-knot operators σ_pp / σ_nn ARE structurally\n  active at magic shells, plus the refined open question\n  pointing at `tr_M(σ_{shell})` (full Markov trace of the\n  shell sub-braid) instead of the simple product-volume\n  convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_pair_knot_markov_trace_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_pair_knot_markov_trace_form","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L350-L380","doc":"**Pair-knot Markov-trace refinement refutation.** Replacing the\nsimple product `|V̂_pair| = ∏ |V̂_i|` with the canonical Markov\ntrace `|V̂_pair| = |tr_M(σ_{i_1} ... σ_{i_k})|` of the magic-shell\nsub-braid as a single Hecke element (via Hoefsmit seminormal at\nq_0) — plus the full Frobenius Gram `G_ij = tr_M(σ_i σ_j)` in\nthe operator-selection LP, plus the SDP dual via cvxpy / SCS —\nSTILL fails the falsifiability criterion: worst-atom abs error\n996.6% on tritium, ³He at `+154%`.\n\nTwo positive structural findings (recorded for downstream use):\n* Both LP and SDP achieve strong duality at the full Gram\n  (LP gap ≤ 10⁻¹⁵; SDP gap ≤ 10⁻⁶ via SCS).\n* **Z=2 / N=2 isospin symmetry restored at the Markov-trace\n  level**: `tr_M(σ_pp) = tr_M(σ_nn) = 0.0622` exactly, vs the\n  asymmetric Δ_shell calibration under product-volume.  The\n  1.326× ratio in family 5 was a product-volume artifact, not\n  a real symmetry breaking.\n\nStructural conclusion (CLOSURE): the brane-tower formula's\nΦ_q-truncated tower at any operator-volume convention (product,\ngeometric mean, OR canonical Markov trace) overshoots at the\nAME light-isotope scale.  The ³He gap is NOT an operator-volume\nissue — it is a structural deficit of the brane-tower formula\nitself at the A=3 / n_0=9 / 2-near-pole regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_pair_knot_product_volume_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_pair_knot_product_volume_form","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L323-L348","doc":"**Pair-knot product-volume convention refutation.** Replacing\nper-generator Φ_q sums over the magic-shell intra-block by a\nsingle composite Φ_q(|V̂_pair|) with\n`|V̂_pair| = ∏_{i ∈ shell} |V̂_i|` (Hopf-link / categorical-product\nconvention) FAILS the falsifiability criterion: worst-atom abs\nerror 1056.9% on tritium under the paired tower.\n\nNotable structural finding (positive): ⁴He at `-19.43%` is the\nclosest closure achieved by any probed form, and the operator-\nselection LP dual confirms (strong duality, gap = 0) that the\npair-knot composite operators σ_pp / σ_nn are in the active set\nEXACTLY at magic-shell atoms — see\n`lpDualActiveSetIncludesPairKnotAtMagicShells`.  The LP-dual\nevidence indicates the pair-knot is structurally privileged at\nZ=2 / N=2; the FAILURE of the product-volume convention to\nclose points at a richer composite-volume operator (e.g.\n`tr_M(σ_{i_1} ... σ_{i_k})` of the shell sub-braid as a single\nHecke element via Hoefsmit seminormal) — pursued in the\nrefinement theorem below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_multiplicity_and_type_b_forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_multiplicity_and_type_b_forms","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L301-L321","doc":"**Multiplicity-refined + Type-B-folded-crystal `n_⋆` refutation.**\nFour substrate-derived per-atom rules (mult-shifted Hecke,\nmult-truncated Hecke, Type-B-folded self-dual partition diagonal\ndepth, combined) in BOTH scalar and operator-valued tower\nformulations were probed.  The best — R2 mult-truncated in\noperator-valued form — correctly identifies D and T per-atom\nsweet spots from substrate data alone (a structurally\ninformative finding) but cannot close ³He at any per-atom\nn_⋆.  Worst-atom abs error 55.97% > 10% threshold.\n\nThis refutation closes the multiplicity-refined open branch\nthat was queued in the operator-valued probe section.  The\nopen path now points BEYOND the n_⋆ choice: the ³He binding\ngap is a structural deficit of the brane-tower formula at\nA=3 / n_0=9 / 2-near-pole regime, not a level-selection\nfailure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lpDualActiveSetIncludesPairKnotAtMagicShells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lpDualActiveSetIncludesPairKnotAtMagicShells","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L291-L299","doc":"The LP-dual active set on the canonical magic-shell atoms\nmatches the substrate's magic-shell signature: pair-knot\noperators are active iff the corresponding magic-number\ncondition is satisfied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.magicShellActiveSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.magicShellActiveSet","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L282-L289","doc":"Active-set pattern at each canonical (Z, N) atom, per the LP-dual\nwitness on the operator-valued tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqLPDualActiveSet.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqLPDualActiveSet.decEq","kind":"def","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L280-L280","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqLPDualActiveSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqLPDualActiveSet","kind":"instance","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L280-L280","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet.hasSigmaNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet.hasSigmaNN","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L279-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet.hasSigmaPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet.hasSigmaPP","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L278-L278","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet.mk","kind":"ctor","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L277-L277","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LPDualActiveSet","kind":"structure","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L258-L280","doc":"Structural finding from the same pair-knot witness: the\n**operator-selection LP dual** (per `prop:operator-selection-lp`\nand AGENTS.md \"LP / SDP duals — first-class infra\") selects\nthe pair-knot composite operators `σ_{pp}` / `σ_{nn}` in the\nactive set EXACTLY for magic-shell atoms.\n\nActive sets per atom (operator-selection LP, diagonal Frobenius\nGram, strong duality verified gap = 0):\n  D (no magic):           σ_pp, σ_nn absent (no pair-knot in basis)\n  T (N=2 magic):          σ_nn active\n  ³He (Z=2 magic):        σ_pp active\n  ⁴He (Z=2 + N=2 magic):  both σ_pp and σ_nn active\n\nThis is the operator-level signature that pair-knot composites\nare structurally distinguishable from per-generator operators\nat exactly the magic configurations.  A boolean record that the\nLP-dual produced this active-set pattern (used by audit\ntooling; carries no logical content beyond what the witness\nasserts). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessPairKnotMarkovTraceMaxAbsErrPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessPairKnotMarkovTraceMaxAbsErrPct","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L241-L256","doc":"Witness-recorded worst-atom abs error under the **refined\npair-knot probe** with canonical Markov-trace composite volume\n`|V̂_shell| = |tr_M(σ_{i_1} σ_{i_2} σ_{i_3} σ_{i_4})|` (Hoefsmit\nseminormal at q_0) plus the full Frobenius Gram\n`G_ij = tr_M(σ_i σ_j)` in the operator-selection LP, with the\nSDP dual via cvxpy / SCS.\n\nBoth LP and SDP achieve strong duality (gap ≤ 10⁻⁶) but the\nrefined pair-knot tower at the per-atom n_⋆ from family 4 still\novershoots: D `+696%`, T `+997%`, ³He `+154%`.  Worst-atom\n`996.6%` on tritium.\n\nSource:\n`computations/probe-phiq-pair-knot-markov-trace.witness.json`\n(computed `2026-05-11`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessPairKnotProductVolumeMaxAbsErrPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessPairKnotProductVolumeMaxAbsErrPct","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L227-L239","doc":"Witness-recorded worst-atom abs error under the\n**pair-knot magic-shell** probe with simple product-volume\nconvention `|V̂_shell| = ∏_{i ∈ shell} |V̂_i|`.  Closest atom\nis ⁴He at `-19.43%` (doubly magic Z=N=2; best closure across\nall probes), but ³He at `+218.7%`, T at `+1056.9%`, D at\n`+696.2%`.  The Z=2 / N=2 magic-shell symmetry fails:\nΔ_shell(Z=2) = -16.88 MeV from ³He, Δ_shell(N=2) = +22.38 MeV\nfrom ⁴He — opposite signs, 1.326× ratio.\n\nSource:\n`computations/probe-phiq-pair-knot-magic-shell.witness.json`\n(computed `2026-05-11`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessMultiplicityBestMaxAbsErrPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessMultiplicityBestMaxAbsErrPct","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L210-L225","doc":"Witness-recorded best-rule max-relative-error under the\nsubstrate-derived multiplicity / Type-B-folded-crystal-depth\nprobe (`probe_phiq_multiplicity_refined.py`, four rules R1–R4\nin both scalar and operator-valued forms).  The best rule is\n`R2 mult-truncated, op` (n_⋆(𝔥) = max(1, ⌊k_Hecke / m_max⌋)\nwith per-eigenvalue operator-valued tower).  It identifies the\nper-atom optimal truncation depth from substrate data alone for\nD (n_⋆=1, err -6.87%) and T (n_⋆=2, err -8.00%), but the\n³He residual at n_⋆=1 is -55.97% — the worst-atom abs error\nis therefore `55.97%` ≈ `56.0%`.  Structural blocker is the\n³He gap itself, not the n_⋆ choice.\n\nSource:\n`computations/probe-phiq-multiplicity-refined.witness.json`\n(computed `2026-05-11`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nStar_scalar_eigenvalue_form_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nStar_scalar_eigenvalue_form_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L195-L208","doc":"**Scalar-eigenvalue `n_⋆` refutation (combined).** Both probed\nscalar-eigenvalue substrate families — uniform-`k` and\n`ℓ · n₀ + k` — exceed the `10%` falsifiability threshold. By the\nconjecture's own criterion, the **scalar-eigenvalue** existence\nclaim is refuted.  Note: the strictly-stronger operator-valued\nrefutation below (per-eigenvalue, signed, operator-trace) also\nfails, so the `n_⋆` existence claim is refuted across every\nempirically probed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_per_eigenvalue_operator_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_per_eigenvalue_operator_form","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L171-L193","doc":"**Operator-valued `n_⋆` refutation (per-eigenvalue form).**\nThe canonical convolution-aware promotion — Φ_q applied to each\neigenvalue μ_a^(λ) of the braid operator ρ_λ(β) in each Hecke\nirrep V_λ, summed via the operator trace `tr_λ`, then Wedderburn-\nweighted by signed `y_λ(q₀)`, with `|·|` only at the\nbinding-formula level — fails the falsifiability criterion at\nevery uniform `k`. Best case `k = 1` leaves max abs error\n`64.75%` on tritium, an order of magnitude above the `10%`\nthreshold.\n\nNote: per-atom optimal `k` values DO achieve closure individually\n(D at `k=1`: `-6.87%`; T at `k=2`: `-8.00%`), but ³He cannot be\nclosed at any uniform `k`. The conjecture's falsifiability\ncriterion forbids per-atom retuning (\"does not constitute\nprogress\"), so the operator-valued `n_⋆` existence claim is\nrefuted under this canonical promotion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_scalar_ell_n0_k_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_scalar_ell_n0_k_form","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L161-L169","doc":"**Scalar-eigenvalue `n_⋆` refutation (`ℓ · n₀ + k` family).** The\nproposed additive rule from `conj:brane-level-selection`\novershoots `³He` by six orders of magnitude — refutation is\nimmediate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_scalar_uniform_k_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witness_refutes_scalar_uniform_k_form","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L151-L159","doc":"**Scalar-eigenvalue `n_⋆` refutation (uniform-`k` family).** The\nbest uniform-depth candidate (`k = 2`, subtractive form) leaves a\n`+134%` residual on `³He` — an order of magnitude above the\nfalsifiability threshold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessPerEigenvalueOperatorBestMaxAbsErrPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessPerEigenvalueOperatorBestMaxAbsErrPct","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L126-L149","doc":"Witness-recorded best-case max-relative-error under the\n**per-eigenvalue, signed, operator-trace** Wedderburn promotion,\n`tower_op^(k)(β) = |Σ_λ y_λ(q₀) · tr_λ(Φ_q^{[≤k]}(ρ_λ(β)))|`,\nwhere ρ_λ(β) is the braid operator in irrep V_λ (numerical\nmatrix via Hoefsmit seminormal at q₀), Φ_q is applied per\neigenvalue μ_a^(λ), and the operator trace `tr_λ` sums them.\n\nMin-over-k of the max-over-atom absolute error is `64.75%` at\n`k = 1`. Notable per-atom: D at `k=1` lands at `-6.87%` (within\n10%), T at `k=2` lands at `-8.00%` (within 10%), but ³He never\ngets within 50% at any uniform k — there is no single `k` that\ncloses all three simultaneously.\n\nThis is the *canonical* operator-valued promotion: it addresses\nthe three normalization issues with the prior\n`_avg_chi_over_classical_dim` variant — classical→quantum dim\n(resolved structurally by using operator trace), absolute→signed\nχ (resolved by complex Φ_q + final |·|), mean→per-eigenvalue Φ_q\n(resolved directly by `tr_λ` of Φ_q applied to ρ_λ).\n\nSource:\n`computations/probe-phiq-operator-valued.witness.json`\n(computed `2026-05-11`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessNStarRuleMaxErrPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessNStarRuleMaxErrPct","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L116-L124","doc":"Witness-recorded worst-case relative error for the\n`n_⋆ = ℓ · n₀ + k` per-atom rule (also scalar-eigenvalue form)\nat `(n_⋆^D, n_⋆^T, n_⋆^³He) = (14, 27, 20)` (subtractive form).\nMaximum is on `³He` at `+1.18 × 10^6 %`.\n\nSource:\n`computations/probe-phiq-n-star-rule.witness.json`\n(computed `2026-05-09`, `commitSha c8f9603d…`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.witnessUniformKBestMaxErrPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.witnessUniformKBestMaxErrPct","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L105-L114","doc":"Witness-recorded worst-case relative error (subtractive form) at\nthe best uniform truncation depth `k = 2` under the\n**scalar-eigenvalue** form: Φ_q evaluated at scalar\nper-generator volumes `|V̂_i|`, then summed.  Maximum is on\n`³He` at `+134%`.\n\nSource:\n`computations/probe-phiq-uniform-k.witness.json`\n(computed `2026-04-29`, `commitSha 95ed3374…`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.falsifiabilityThresholdPct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.falsifiabilityThresholdPct","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L98-L103","doc":"Falsifiability threshold from the conjecture's `## Falsifiability`\nsection: a candidate `n_⋆` rule must close all three AME light\nisotopes to within `~5%` without per-atom retuning. We use the\n`10%` bound below to remain robust against rounding in the\nwitness arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical","kind":"instance","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L56-L66","doc":"**Tautological-recovery skeleton instance.**  Defines\n`recoversBinding` as the constant `True` predicate; under this\ninterpretation `recovery_holds` closes by `trivial`.  Encodes\nnone of the conjectural recovery content (no per-atom binding\nenergies are checked) but discharges the §3b-cond hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.recovery_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.recovery_holds","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The recovery assertion holds for all confined particles in the model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.recoversBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.recoversBinding","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The cyclotomic projection at `nStar` recovers the empirical binding\nenergy `B_target` up to relative error `eps`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.nStar_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.nStar_pos","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.nStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.nStar","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The canonical cyclotomic truncation level for a confined particle\nwith confinement level `ell`, strand count `n₀`, and GB grade `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerZHabiro","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.lean#L36-L54","doc":"**BraneTowerZHabiro** — the conjectural class.\n\nAn instance for strand count `n₀` and substrate `q` asserts that\nthe brane-tower partial sums converge in the `z`-Habiro topology\nand that a structural level-selection rule `nStar` exists which\nrecovers empirical binding energies without per-atom calibration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:brane-tower-z-habiro","label":"conj:brane-tower-z-habiro","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brane-tower-z-habiro.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}